.TH SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_GAMECUBE_DEVICES_EXCLUDED 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_GAMECUBE_DEVICES_EXCLUDED \- A variable containing a list of devices known not to have a GameCube form factor.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_GAMECUBE_DEVICES_EXCLUDED \(dqSDL_JOYSTICK_GAMECUBE_DEVICES_EXCLUDED\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This will override
.BR SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_GAMECUBE_DEVICES
and the built in device list\[char46]
.PP
The format of the string is a comma separated list of USB VID/PID pairs in hexadecimal form, e\[char46]g\[char46]
.PP
.BR 0xAAAA/0xBBBB,0xCCCC/0xDDDD
.PP
The variable can also take the form of \(dq@file\(dq, in which case the named file will be loaded and interpreted as the value of the variable\[char46]
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

